// Copy to Local.xcconfig for per-machine build settings. That file is
// gitignored; this example is not.
//
// Why this exists: if the repo lives in an iCloud-synced folder (~/Documents,
// ~/Desktop), Xcode code signing fails on extended attributes that the sync
// daemon attaches to files under the build directory. Redirecting the build
// output outside the synced tree avoids it.
//
// WARNING: overriding FLUTTER_BUILD_DIR breaks the iOS build.
//
// Flutter writes native assets under the default build/ directory, but Xcode
// then looks for them in the overridden location and fails:
//
//   Exception: The native assets specification at .../NativeAssetsManifest.json
//   references objective_c, which was not found in <overridden dir>/native_assets/ios/
//
// So this particular override cannot be used for iOS. It is kept here as a
// record of what was tried. The real fix for the iCloud signing problem is to
// move the repo out of the synced tree entirely — which also stops the
// conflict copies described in the README.
//
// The path would be relative to ios/Flutter/.
//
// FLUTTER_BUILD_DIR=../../../../private/tmp/shohoj_flutter_build
